From ac8a365e83cfd133347ed4ac80bb3101f7865875 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:22:23 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] ui: Add password and locked states for platform providers

Platform passkey providers (transport `Internal`) can ask for the user's
login password in place of, or in addition to, a biometric check, and
they can be locked until the user unlocks their key store. Neither case
has a matching event yet.

Add two background events and one UI event to the UI Control API:

- NotifyNeedsPassword(session, incorrect, options) asks the UI to collect
  the password. `incorrect` is true when the provider rejected the
  previous one.
- NotifyInternalLocked(session, options) tells the UI that the provider
  cannot be used until it is unlocked.
- The PasswordEntered(session, password_fd, options) signal returns the
  password in a memfd_secret, like ClientPinEntered does for PINs.

The reference UI reuses the PIN entry for the password and sends it with
PasswordEntered while a password prompt is open. The daemon side only
logs a stray password for now; routing it to a provider comes with the
provider support.
